n $s$ is $x$, which forces $G.\\\\mathrm{Adj}(x, x)$, contradicting the irreflexivity of adjacency in simple graphs.\\n\\nTherefore, any total dominating set $s \\\\subseteq V$ must satisfy $|s| \\\\ge 2$.\\nSince `GraphCalc.HasTotalDominationNumber G` guarantees the existence of at least one total dominating set in $V$, the set of cardinalities of total dominating sets is nonempty. The computable invariant `GraphCalc.totalDominationNumber G`, defined via `GraphCalc.minCard`, takes the minimum over this nonempty set of cardinalities (and falls back to 0 only when empty). Because every total d\n<truncated 816 bytes>","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_9e476a83\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Write REPORT.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
